This article aims to verify to what extent patents granted to the pharmaceutical industry, for the protection of medicines, fulfil the social function of intellectual property. It seeks to compare the benefits brought to society and to pharmaceutical industries by medicine patents, and to analyse the possibility of applying the safeguard measures available in Brazilian legislation in the event of non-compliance with the social function of said patents.
